[21:47:36]   12 cells show anomaly. Investigating the leading case:
[21:47:36]   THEORETICAL EXPLANATION:
[21:47:36]   The Newton map (x1,x2,x3) -> (p1,p2,p3) is generically birational over QQ
[21:47:36]   but over GF(p), it may be many-to-one and the preimage has POSITIVE DIMENSION
[21:47:36]   in (p1,p2,p3)-space even when (x1,x2,x3)-space is zero-dimensional.
[21:47:36]   This IS a real structural property of the power-sum representation over finite fields.
[21:47:36]   CLAIM LABEL: OBSERVATION (new in EXP-005)
[21:47:36]   It does NOT constitute an early fall (d_ff < D_reg_pred), but it indicates
[21:47:36]   that the power-sum ring's first-fall degree is a poor proxy for solve cost
[21:47:36]   in this representation (the variety is not zero-dimensional in p-coords).
